    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1073">

                <pb facs="1052" n="954" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg954"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Loomis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 344.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 444, of the 17th ultimo, stating that Dr. Rojas Paul, a former president of
                    Venezuela, is anxious to preserve the Cuban citizenship of an adopted daughter
                    who is a native of that island.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say that the question will be one for the determination of the
                    Cuban authorities when a definitive government shall be established in Cuba.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
